the new head of the bureau of alcohol  tobacco firearms and explosives tells  cbs news he has a plan to tackle  america's gun violence epidemic steve  detelbeck was sworn in yesterday as the  atf's first permanent director in more  than seven years a short time later he  sat down for an exclusive interview with  cbs evening news anchor and managing  editor noah o'donnell  i think it'd be naive for me to sit here  and say to you that  i would get confirmed as atf director  and this this constant drumbeat of gun  violence is going to stop to me what we  have to do is focus on addressing the  problem it's time to push the we got to  get to work button not the panic button  will there be more uvaldis uh it's it's  just a horrible question for you to even  have to ask right but the truth of the  matter is is that there have been just  incident after incident for a long  period of time so we have to work hard  to  try to make sure there aren't but i  think the reality is there's going to be  serious gun crime  that we have to work on at atf  and you can see more of nora's interview  with steve detelbach on cbsnews.com
 

